{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-15479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the coefficient of $(x+1)^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ about $x=-1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-15479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The coefficient of $(x+1)^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(-1).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\frac{24}{{x}^{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(-1),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(-1)=-\\frac{24}{(-1)^{5}}=-\\frac{24}{(-1)}=24.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(-1)=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot 24=\\frac{24}{6}=4.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x+1)^{3}$ is $4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-15479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d187f4c6935d1871677f80f2da5e85b2423abe9481ef47b4727c362f7ea4b2fd"} {"question" "q-15479" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-15479" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-15479" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-15484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the coefficient of $(x+\\pi )^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ about $x=-\\pi ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-15484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The coefficient of $(x+\\pi )^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(-\\pi ).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(-\\pi ),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(-\\pi )=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(-\\pi )=\\frac{1}{3!}\\cdot 1=\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of $(x+\\pi )^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-15484" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d187f4c6935d1871677f80f2da5e85b2423abe9481ef47b4727c362f7ea4b2fd"} {"question" "q-15484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-15484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-15484" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-126359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ in the third-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)=\\frac{1}{1-x}$ about $x=0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-126359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{(3)}(0).$ Let's compute the necessary derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{1}{1-x} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{1}{(1-x)^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =\\frac{2}{(1-x)^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\frac{6}{(1-x)^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate ${f}^{‴}(0),$ which gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{6}{(1-0)^{4}}=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3!}{f}^{‴}(0)=\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 6=1.\n$$\n\nSo the coefficient of ${x}^{3}$ is $1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-126359" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d187f4c6935d1871677f80f2da5e85b2423abe9481ef47b4727c362f7ea4b2fd"} {"question" "q-126359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-126359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-126359" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-351859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)={e}^{-2x}$ about $x=0.$\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=1-2x\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-351859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & f(0) & ={e}^{-0}=1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-2{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =-2{e}^{-0}=-2 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =4{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =4{e}^{-0}=4 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =-8{e}^{-2x} & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =-8{e}^{-0}=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results for $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0)$ into our third-degree Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =1-2\\cdot x+4\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-8\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =1-2x+2{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-351859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d187f4c6935d1871677f80f2da5e85b2423abe9481ef47b4727c362f7ea4b2fd"} {"question" "q-351859" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-351859" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x^2-\\frac{4}{3}x^3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-351980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the third-degree Taylor polynomial ${P}_{3}(x)$ of $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ about $x=0.$ Do  not round the answer.\n\n${P}_{3}(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}\n${x}^{2}\\,+$\n{{field-3}}\n${x}^{3}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-351980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the third-degree Taylor polynomial about $x=0,$ we plug $a=0$ into the general formula to give\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!} \\\\  & =f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)x+{f}^{″}(0)\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+{f}^{‴}(0)\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to compute $f(0),$ ${f}^{′}(0),$ ${f}^{″}(0),$ and ${f}^{‴}(0),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & f(0) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}(0) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}(0) & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}(0) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0+\\frac{\\pi }{3})=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we plug the results into our Taylor polynomial. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{3}(x) & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x+(-\\frac{1}{2})\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{12}{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-351980" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d187f4c6935d1871677f80f2da5e85b2423abe9481ef47b4727c362f7ea4b2fd"} {"question" "q-351980" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-351980" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa84a9d737cad2bab78"} {"question" "q-351980" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14054465/state.json" "file_sha256" "752512c22dce5456b62f3ed342a74e211f086c524e43bfa8